column2:
Om, salutation to you, object of the highest truth, gross and subtle, perishable and imperishable, manifest and unmanifest, beyond the digits, lord of all, stainless;
vishnupurana:20:10	you who colour the gunas, support of the gunas, whose self is without gunas, abiding in the gunas, with form and formless, of great form, of subtle form, evident and hidden;
vishnupurana:20:11	whose self is of terrible and gentle form, made of knowledge and ignorance, Achyuta, whose true being is existent and non-existent, producer of existent and non-existent being;
vishnupurana:20:12	eternal and non-eternal, whose self is the manifold world, stainless refuge beyond the manifold, one and many, salutation to you, Vasudeva, first cause.
vishnupurana:20:13	He who is gross and subtle, manifest and shining, who is all beings and yet not all beings, from whom, who is not the cause of the universe, this universe is — salutation to that Supreme Person.
